## Findings

**(c) Implementation looks wrong: footer is not actually re-themed by the Xeniapolis override**

Spec: *"the Xeniapolis palette overrides the default across the entire rendered page — shared chrome (nav, sidebar, footer) included, not just the article body — while browsing that section."* (also restated verbatim in ADR-0002 line 27 and `about-section-theming.md` line 37: *"applied high enough in the docs layout tree to wrap shared chrome (nav, sidebar, footer) as well as the article body"*).

Tracing the actual DOM nesting: `src/app/layout.tsx` renders `<body><RootProvider>{children}</RootProvider><Footer /></body>` — the `Footer` is a **sibling** of `RootProvider`, not a descendant. The `data-section="xeniapolis"` attribute is applied via `containerProps` on `DocsLayout`'s `slots.container` (confirmed in `node_modules/@fumadocs/base-ui/dist/layouts/docs/client.js`), which lives deep inside `RootProvider`'s children — several levels below where `Footer` sits. CSS custom-property cascade only flows to descendants, so `--background`/`--primary`/etc. redefined under `[data-section='xeniapolis']` never reach `Footer`. Nav and sidebar *are* correctly inside that container (confirmed via the same client.js trace and `layout.config.tsx`), so those two are fine — but the footer will keep rendering in the Atelier palette on Xeniapolis pages, contradicting the explicit "footer included" claim in the spec, ADR-0002, and the explanation doc. This looks like a real gap between the documented design and the shipped code, not merely an unverified manual-check item.

**(a) Missing/partial:** Nothing else missing — palette replacement, root/dark palettes, `data-section` derivation via `getNodeMeta()`/`PathUtils.dirname()`, and independent `--atelier-color`/`--xeniapolis-color` wiring at `:root` (outside the `[data-section]` scope, confirmed by reading `globals.css`) are all present and match the spec's description.

**(b) Scope creep:** None found. The `layout.tsx` file move to `[[...slug]]/` and the `findPath`/`getPageSection` helper are necessitated by needing route `params`, consistent with the spec's "derived per-current-page" requirement, not additive scope.

**Palette sanity check:** both `:root`/`.dark` (Atelier) and `[data-section='xeniapolis']`/dark-compound (Xeniapolis) define full light+dark variants, all `oklch(...)` syntax is well-formed, and primary hues are clearly distinct (Atelier ~45° orange/brown vs. Xeniapolis ~260-265° blue/violet) — internally reasonable.

**Not independently verifiable here:** `pnpm build` (OOM ceiling in this sandbox, pre-existing/unrelated) and the manual light/dark + section-browsing smoke check (no browser available).The spec review surfaced a potential real gap: the footer might sit outside the `data-section` scope. Let me verify this directly before acting on it.Confirmed — `Footer` is a sibling of `RootProvider` in `src/app/layout.tsx:29-40`, so it sits outside wherever `data-section` gets applied inside the docs tree. This is a real, spec-contradicting gap (the issue and ADR explicitly call out "footer included"). Let me look at the broader layout structure before deciding on a fix.
